# Domain enums

Keep each enum in its own PascalCase file beside the model that uses it, for example `Orders/OrderStatus.cs`. Match the file-scoped namespace to that business area.
Assign each member an explicit integer. For a new sequence, start at zero with the appropriate initial value. Preserve assigned numbers when a stored or published enum evolves.
Use three-line Russian summaries on the type and each member. Separate members with a blank line and keep the trailing comma.

```csharp
namespace Catalog.Domain.Orders;

/// <summary>
/// Состояние заказа.
/// </summary>
public enum OrderStatus
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Черновик заказа.
    /// </summary>
    Draft = 0,

    /// <summary>
    /// Заказ принят.
    /// </summary>
    Accepted = 1,
}
```
